 of carbon reduction that's  required so it's very dramatic the the  scale of emissions reduction that's  needed and therefore we do need to keep  very regular track we need to have that  kind of accountability and importantly  we also need to identify the areas where  we are making progress and why and also  the areas in which we're not  and particularly in the areas in which  we're really not making progress and  again i would i would point to you know  the 80 of energy use outside of the  power sector as being an area that needs  a lot of attention we need to develop  strategies for decarbonizing um  those sectors of the economy um that  have tended to be neglected because we  don't have very good answers and as  these developing countries particularly  begin to industrialize and grow their  economies it's very likely that their  energy consumption will increase in  those sectors as they want to build  hundreds of new schools and hundreds of  new hospitals and build out their  industrial capability um that they may  quickly find that themselves in a very  similar  kind of energy intensive carbon  intensive economy that we also  find ourselves in the existing developed  country thank you kirsty i'm so sorry we  have run out of time it was such a  pleasure to talk to you and hopefully  we'll have you back on the show very  very soon um well that's all from us  thank you very much for watching we will  see you next time bye  [Music]

